    "created_at": "2026-09-16T18:18:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-16T18:18:18Z",
    "body": "I can confirm that this happens in chrome. Safari 27 (supports sizes=\"auto\") and Firefox do not have this issue.\n\nn [Blink's `sizes_attribute_parser.cc` at commit d7ee5ded1339638d31ac503f68327d00f70b3901](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/d7ee5ded1339638d31ac503f68327d00f70b3901/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/parser/sizes_attribute_parser.cc#34), `Parse()` returns immediately when it encounters `auto` (lines 34–40). `EffectiveSize()` uses the layout width only while the image is rendered, then falls through to the viewport default (lines 135–157). \n\nThis causes multiple downloads and on websites with very large amounts of auto sized images can cause bandwidth contention for other resources. This is especially true for React applications that mount and unmount images for things like modals, carousels, etc",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
