    "created_at": "2026-09-16T20:55:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T13:52:45Z",
    "body": "I agree it makes sense to not load anything when an auto-size image stops being rendered.\n\n~Not loading anything initially if it's not rendered could cause compat issues at this point, and is not what `sizes` is meant to do. How about assuming a layout size of the `width` and `height` attributes (on the `img` or the selected `source`), if present, otherwise [300x150](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#img-contain-size)?~\n\n~If one wants to avoid an initial wrong load until the element is rendered, `loading=lazy` can be used, or we can revisit [adding `loading=after-layout`](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8007).~\n\nEdit: struck the above, I forgot that auto-sizes requires lazy-loading.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
